  "note": "Election of 21 members for seven wards (three each) on 17 May 1961. Carnmoney, Jordanstown and Whitewell were uncontested; there were contests in Cavehill, Glengormley, Whiteabbey and Whitehouse. The three Labour candidates were returned; the printed Ulster Unionist vote for Gillespie is partly obscured and is read as 574."
